            <ArticleTitle>The Inflammatory Response in Cardiac Surgery. An Up-to-date Overview with the Emphasis on the Role of Heat Shock Proteins (HSPs) 60 and 70.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-99</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.14712/18059694.2017.62</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac surgical operations are associated with the development of a systemic inflammatory response syndrome (SIRS). In most cases, the inflammatory response is apparent only in its subclinical form. In some cases, however, it can become clinically manifest or even life-threatening. This review article presents some new data regarding its biological importance, along with an insight into the recently discovered role played by heat shock proteins 60 and 70.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
